  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "direct": "On the unpatched selected-build path, Setup converts LevelWaterVolumeData.id through System.UInt64.ToString and stores the returned managed string pointer in WaterVolume.waterVolumeId; it also transfers the pointer, pivot, height inputs, and mesh hash. Nonzero id becomes a nonstatic WaterVolumePtr, for which InitMeshMono computes get_planePosition and passes it with the stored hash to GetMesh. GetMesh passes the hash to ResourceManager.TryLoad; an acquired asset reaches WaterSurfaceMeshMono.UpdataMesh and MeshFilter/MeshCollider sharedMesh.",
    "conditional": "For an infinite water row, Setup initializes the ratio amountCurrent/amountMax; GetHeight multiplies that ratio by heightMax and get_planePosition adds the result to pivot. This is an initial requested position if Setup and the unpatched branch execute, not a live transform receipt. Later SetAmount on an infinite volume can call SetInfiniteWaterHeight and _UpdateInfiniteWaterMeshPos, which can call WaterSurfaceMeshMono height setters; execution and final state depend on runtime inputs and guards.",
    "unresolved": "This native contract alone names no concrete scene or hash value. A separately gated LevelData/StringPathHash join names one authored asset and footprint. The initial capture directly observed one selected-volume mesh delivery. A selected Setup-return get_position call can observe actual Transform.position on the same game thread; later selected set_position returns can observe that Mono's own setter path. No installed file proves the selected Mono will Tick, that no other Transform writer exists, that a setup-time position persists until stop, or that a renderer is visible."
  }
}
